# items.rec: every base item, one record each. Order is content: D1 rolls items by walking this table. One schema
# serves every mod; a mod fills in the fields its game uses and leaves the rest out.
# Identity:
#   internal_name     id other files use (classes.rec, stores.rec, quests.rec); required
#   name / short_name the shown name, and the short one that fits the belt
#   icon              icons/items.rec id, e.g. item.dagger
# Where it appears:
#   dlvl              the shallowest dungeon level it drops on (D1's iMinMLvl); max_level the deepest (0: none)
#   out_of_depth_chance / min_level_for_ood   chance to drop above its dlvl, from this dungeon level on
#   drop              IDROP_REGULAR, IDROP_DOUBLE (twice as likely) or IDROP_NEVER (quests and stores only)
#   hidden            true: unseen and out of reach until the hero has true sight (H&H's evidence)
#   cost              its value in gold (D1's iValue)
# What it is (a record names either category or D1's class/item_type):
#   category          potion scroll wand light weapon armor ammo ring food amulet throwable
#   class / location / item_type   D1's ICLASS_ (WEAPON, ARMOR, MISC, GOLD, QUEST), ILOC_ (ONEHAND, TWOHAND,
#                     ARMOR, HELM, RING, AMULET, BELT, UNEQUIPABLE) and ITYPE_ number
#   cursor            D1's inventory graphic number (ICURS_), which also picks its sound (item_sounds.rec)
#   unique_base       UITYPE_ name the unique items (xl_uitem.txt) built on it refer to
#   durability        maximum durability (255: indestructible)
#   requires_strength / requires_magic / requires_dexterity   what the hero needs to use it
#   flags             D1's ISPL_ bits, "ISPL_NONE" or several separated by |
#   misc_id / spell   D1's IMISC_ kind (IMISC_FULLHEAL, IMISC_SCROLL, IMISC_BOOK, IMISC_STAFF, ...) and the SPL_ it casts
# Weapons:
#   weapon_type       sword axe mace bow crossbow shield scythe spear whip dagger sling
#   weapon_damage     a range "2-6" or dice "1d4"
#   weapon_speed / weapon_two_handed / weapon_armor_penetration   attack speed factor, true for two hands, AC ignored
#   ranged_max_range / ranged_accuracy_at_min_range / ranged_accuracy_at_max_range / ranged_projectile_icon
#                     a missile weapon's reach, accuracy (0..1) at either end, and the icon its shot flies with
# Armour:
#   armor_type        helmet cuirass gloves boots cape amulet ring shield defensive_weapon
#   armor_class       a range "3-5" (rolled) or a number
# Throwing:
#   throw_damage      "min-max" damage when thrown; throw_chance_to_break 0..1 that it breaks on landing
#   throw_hit_zone    what a throw hits: target_only, neighbors_only, ray_aoe, bolt_aoe, dijkstra_aoe(n), box_aoe(n), ...
#   throw_on_hit_effect   an effect (effects/targeted.rec) it applies to what it hits
# Light sources:
#   charges           turns a light burns, or uses a wand or scroll has
#   light_color       "R G B" of its light; light_flicker_pattern (fire, smooth, steady, or the brightness per
#                     frame as numbers, e.g. "1.0 0.9 0.8 0.9") and light_flicker_frame_delay (seconds per frame)
# Powers:
#   equip_modifier    what it does while worn: strength, dexterity, intelligence, health, mana, damage, armor_class,
#                     light_radius, attack_speed, steal_health, steal_mana, speed, move_speed; "name(n)" gives n,
#                     a bare name rolls up to the item level; repeatable
#   untargeted_action / targeted_action   the effect (effects/*.rec) using it triggers
#
# Heaven&Hell's items in the unified items.rec schema every mod uses (see defs.Item), ported from
# the game's own items/{weapons,armor,accessory,potions,scrolls,light,misc,unique_items}.rec.
#
# The only field that changed shape: icon was a raw sprite-sheet number in the item record and is now
# an icon ID this mod defines in icons/items.rec, the same convention D1's items use. Everything else
# was already the unified schema -- this schema IS H&H's, which is why D1's table was converted to it
# and not the other way round.
#
# The records are in source-file order; the last block is unique_items.rec. Nothing places uniques
# differently yet: the engine has no H&H item placement on this branch.

